      "question_id": "Q2",
      "question": "Which internal roles are required to attend the vendor meeting, and who is responsible for setting and distributing the agenda beforehand?",
      "answer": "The equipment engineer and a meeting organizer are the key internal participants, alongside the vendor representative. Preparing the agenda and the equipment issue summary beforehand falls to the equipment engineer. The organizer then handles the logistics of getting the meeting on the calendar and distributing the materials."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q3",
      "question": "In what format is the meeting discussion captured — for example, a structured template, free-text notes, or a recording — and where is that output stored after the meeting?",
      "answer": "Decisions and open questions are captured in meeting notes by the organizer during the session. The resulting summary is stored in a shared document repository. The specific format — template versus free text — is not specified in the available information."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q4",
      "question": "How are action items identified from the meeting output — does one designated person extract them manually, or is there a defined process or template that guides what qualifies as an action item?",
      "answer": "The organizer records decisions and open questions during the meeting, and from that output a manager identifies and assigns action items to responsible parties with due dates. Whether a formal template guides what qualifies as an action item is not specified."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q5",
      "question": "What tool or system is used to track action items after they are assigned, and is there a standard deadline or response window that applies to each item?",
      "answer": "A dedicated action-item tracking tool is used to monitor progress after assignments are made. Due dates are set per item during the assignment step, so deadlines are item-specific rather than governed by a single universal response window. A standard default timeframe is not specified."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q6",
      "question": "What criteria must be met for an action item to be considered closed, and what happens if an item is not resolved within the expected timeframe — is there a defined escalation path?",
      "answer": "Closure criteria are not explicitly specified. However, a missed follow-up deadline is recognized as an exception in the process, implying that overdue items are flagged. A formal escalation path for unresolved items is not described in the available information."
    }
  ]
